data/schema-subclasses.json
---------------------------

NOT covered by the AGPL-3.0 above.

Derived from the schema.org vocabulary, which is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License version 3.0:

    https://schema.org/docs/terms.html
    http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/

The file contains the rdfs:subClassOf edges of the vocabulary with all other
content removed. As a derivative of a CC BY-SA 3.0 work it is itself licensed
CC BY-SA 3.0.

Attribution: schema.org — https://schema.org/

The two licences sit side by side as mere aggregation. Neither reaches the
other: the vocabulary derivative is data read at runtime, not a component
linked into the program.

Regenerate with:

    node tools/fetch-schema-hierarchy.ts

The file records the SHA-256 of the exact source document it was derived from,
so the derivation is verifiable.

data/google-rich-results.json
-----------------------------

Covered by the AGPL-3.0 above. Written for this project; no third-party text is
reproduced in it.

It records which properties Google documents as required or recommended for each
rich-result feature. Those are facts about a published specification rather than
expression, and every entry cites the Google page it was read from so the claim
can be checked at source:

    https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/

Google's developer documentation is licensed CC BY 4.0. Nothing here copies it —
the field lists are data and the surrounding prose is original — but the
attribution is recorded because the source deserves naming.
